# How to cite this software, read by GitHub ("Cite this repository"). Keep the version in step
# with pyproject.toml. The data are not in this repository: cite the Scottish Government dataset
# as the README says.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the data: Scottish Government, Domestic Energy Performance Certificates, extended historic dataset (data.gov.scot), Open Government Licence v3.0."
title: "epc-scotland: Scottish domestic EPCs for SQL Server"
abstract: >-
  A CLI pipeline that puts every certificate of the Scottish Government's extended historic
  extract of domestic Energy Performance Certificates into one SQL Server table, values exactly
  as published, from hash-pinned sources, with typed copies for joining by UPRN and date and a
  row digest that a load is checked against. The recipe is public; the built table is not.
authors:
  - family-names: Tinti
    given-names: Michele
    affiliation: "Health Informatics Centre (HIC), University of Dundee"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0051-017X"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtinti/epc-scotland"
keywords:
  - Energy Performance Certificate
  - EPC
  - UPRN
  - SQL Server
  - data linkage
  - Scotland
